<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Reeve returns two weeks after his first visit and is seen by Dr. Kovac of physical medicine and rehabilitation on the same day. He uses the diaphragm pacer for two hours twice a day, as the pacing team advised, and the ventilator the rest of the time; he tires toward the end of each session but his saturation stays at 96 to 97%. His secretions are thin and his nurses suction a few times a day and use the cough-assist device each morning. His skin has stayed intact. His bowel program has worked each morning, and his catheter drains well. He has had no pounding headaches, flushing or sweating above the injury. His neck and shoulders ache after long days in the chair. He has continued stimulated cycling three times a week. All of his regular nurses have now been trained in the autonomic dysreflexia plan, and he carries the wallet card. He had his bone density scan and kidney and bladder ultrasound this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Breathing</td><td>Pacer two hours twice a day; ventilator otherwise; saturation 96 to 97% on the pacer</td></tr><tr><td>Autonomic dysreflexia</td><td>No episodes; plan and wallet card in place; nurses trained</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>Intact</td></tr><tr><td>Bladder and bowel</td><td>Catheter draining well; bowel program effective</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>Neck and shoulder aching after long days</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
